# Casparel mobile — example environment
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) for local builds, or set these as EAS
# environment variables / secrets for `eas build`.

# ── RevenueCat (public SDK keys — safe to ship in the client bundle) ──────────
# Development and preview builds use RevenueCat Test Store. Production builds
# use the matching platform key. Keep real values in local/EAS secrets; never
# commit them. Test Store public keys start with `test_` and must never ship in
# a production build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_TEST_KEY=test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_USE_TEST_STORE=true

# ── Google Mobile Ads (public IDs — safe to ship in the client bundle) ───────
# Development/preview must use Google's sample units. Production must set this
# to false and provide the real app + placement IDs in the EAS production
# environment. The release check rejects Google's sample publisher in a
# production build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADS_USE_TEST_IDS=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_ANDROID_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~yyyyyyyyyy
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_IOS_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~yyyyyyyyyy
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_ANDROID_DASHBOARD_UNIT_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx/yyyyyyyyyy

# ── API host ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An override, not a requirement: utils/api-host.ts defaults to casparel.com,
# so a build that forgets this still talks to production instead of to nothing.
# Every eas.json profile sets it explicitly; set it here to point a local run
# at somewhere else. The scheme and any trailing slash are optional.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=staging.casparel.com
